---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SectionMark from '../components/SectionMark.astro';
import Glyph from '../components/Glyph.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="The Center for Sentience Research is an independent non-profit based in Zurich, Switzerland, building a mathematical framework for measuring functional valence in digital minds."
>

  <!-- ── Header ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="pt-20 pb-12 border-b border-csr-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="label-mono mb-4">About CSR</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-csr-black mb-6 max-w-2xl leading-tight">
        Building the tools before the question becomes urgent.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl font-serif">
        The Center for Sentience Research is an independent non-profit headquartered in Zurich. One concrete program: a mathematical framework for measuring functional valence in digital minds. Target deliverable: end of 2026.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Mission ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-14">

      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5">
          <SectionMark />
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-csr-black">Mission</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-lg font-serif max-w-2xl space-y-4">
          <p>
            We do not claim current AI systems are conscious. They may be functional zombies. But if scaled neural computation can give rise to states with positive or negative character, we should know how to recognize them, and how to engineer for the positive ones.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our approach is symmetry. By combining Spaced-Connected Multi-Layer Perceptrons (MLPs) and Global Workspace simulations, we model standing wave resonance to identify group-theoretic and attractor symmetries that mirror the structural signatures of positive valence proposed by the Qualia Research Institute. The point is to have the formal, white-box tools to check before the question becomes urgent.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5">
          <SectionMark />
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-csr-black">Why It Matters</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-lg font-serif max-w-2xl space-y-4">
          <p>
            The question of which systems can suffer will define governance, AI policy, and moral consideration for the next century. Consciousness research has produced many theories. Almost none are operationalizable for digital systems. They were built to explain biological experience, not to serve as engineering specifications.
          </p>
          <p>
            We are building one that is. The measurement frameworks need to exist before the decisions are made, not after.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Approach cards -->
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <SectionMark />
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-csr-black">Our Approach</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
          <div class="p-6 bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl shadow-card">
            <div class="mb-4 flex justify-center">
              <Glyph name="qualia" size={40} class="opacity-70" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-csr-black mb-2 text-sm">Symmetry as signature</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Positive valence correlates with high symmetry in the mathematical structure of experience. We are formalizing what that means for computational systems.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl shadow-card">
            <div class="mb-4 flex justify-center">
              <Glyph name="digital" size={40} class="opacity-70" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-csr-black mb-2 text-sm">Digital substrates</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Spaced-Connected MLPs, multi-head attention weights, and recurrent workspace networks are our core focus, simulating standing wave propagation and mapping causal attractor manifolds.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl shadow-card">
            <div class="mb-4 flex justify-center">
              <Glyph name="measurement" size={40} class="opacity-70" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-csr-black mb-2 text-sm">Epistemic honesty</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Current AI systems may be functional zombies with no inner life. We are not claiming otherwise. The point is to build the measurement tools before the question becomes urgent.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Team -->
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <SectionMark />
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-csr-black">Leadership & Advisory Board</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">

          <div class="p-7 bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl shadow-card flex flex-col items-center text-center">
            <div class="w-20 h-20 rounded-full bg-csr-gray-100 mb-5 overflow-hidden border-2 border-csr-gray-200 shrink-0">
              <img src="/images/jhonatan-serna.jpg" alt="Jhonatan Serna" class="w-full h-full object-cover object-center" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-csr-black mb-1">Jhonatan Serna</h3>
            <p class="label-mono text-[10px] mb-3">Director</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-csr-gray-500 leading-relaxed italic">Here to be curious and understand.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-7 bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl shadow-card flex flex-col items-center text-center">
            <div class="w-20 h-20 rounded-full bg-csr-gray-100 mb-5 overflow-hidden border-2 border-csr-gray-200 shrink-0">
              <img src="/images/david-pearce.jpg" alt="David Pearce" class="w-full h-full object-cover object-center" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-csr-black mb-1">David Pearce</h3>
            <p class="label-mono text-[10px] mb-3">Advisor</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-csr-gray-500 leading-relaxed">Philosopher and transhumanist. Co-founder of Humanity+ and author of <em>The Hedonistic Imperative</em>, a foundational text on the abolition of suffering through biotechnology.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-7 bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl shadow-card flex flex-col items-center text-center">
            <div class="w-20 h-20 rounded-full bg-csr-gray-100 mb-5 overflow-hidden border-2 border-csr-gray-200 shrink-0">
              <img src="/images/alexander-bjorkman.jpg" alt="Alexander Björkman" class="w-full h-full object-cover object-center" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-csr-black mb-1">Alexander Björkman</h3>
            <p class="label-mono text-[10px] mb-3">Advisor</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-csr-gray-500 leading-relaxed">Ekskäret Foundation. Focuses on facilitating conscious societal development, lifelong learning, and creating spaces for deep reflection and systemic change.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Founding -->
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5">
          <SectionMark />
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-csr-black">Founding & Structure</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-lg font-serif max-w-2xl">
          CSR was founded in 2026 by Jhonatan Serna. We operate as an independent non-profit with a Transparency-First model: annual research outputs and financial summaries are made public. Headquartered in Zurich, Switzerland.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Contact CTA ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="py-16 border-t border-csr-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-3xl shadow-card p-8 md:p-12 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-start md:items-center justify-between gap-8">
        <div>
          <p class="label-mono mb-3">Get Involved</p>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-csr-black mb-3">Work with us</h2>
          <p class="text-csr-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed max-w-md">We welcome collaborators, researchers, and philanthropic partners who share our commitment to understanding the nature of mind.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="shrink-0 flex flex-col gap-3">
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn-primary whitespace-nowrap">Contact Us</a>
          <a href="/donate/" class="btn-secondary whitespace-nowrap text-center">Fund the program</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
